## 🚨 CRITICAL: No Unicode Emojis (Crash Prevention)

**DEADLY EMOJIS (NEVER USE):**
- 🎉 (partypopper) - causes immediate crashes
- 🏆 (trophy) - system instability
- 🚀 (rocket) - serialization failures
- Any Unicode emoji in Python/PS1/logger contexts

**STRICT BAN in these file types:**
- **Python files (.py)** - All Unicode emojis forbidden
- **PowerShell scripts (.ps1)** - All Unicode emojis forbidden
- **Logger messages** - `logger.info("🚀 Started")` → `logger.info("STARTED")`

**FORBIDDEN contexts:**
- Logger messages (`logger.info("🚀 Started")`) - causes crashes and restart loops
- API parameters - serialization failures
- MCP responses - client crashes
- Error messages - encoding failures
- Variable names, function names, comments

**✅ ALLOWED in HTML for pretty UI:**
- Emojis can be used in HTML templates and UI strings
- Web dashboard displays and user-facing content
- README.md and documentation files

**✅ SAFE alternatives:**
- ASCII text only: "Process started" instead of "🚀 Started"
- NO Unicode emojis in Python/PS1/logger contexts EVER

## 🐧 CRITICAL: No Linux Syntax in PowerShell Chats

**🚫 FORBIDDEN in PowerShell environments:**
- `&&` (command chaining)
- `||` (logical OR)
- `|` (pipes)
- `;` (command separators)
- `&` (background)
- `mkdir -p` (use `New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force`)
- `ls -la` (use `Get-ChildItem`)
- `rm -rf` (use `Remove-Item -Recurse -Force`)

**✅ REQUIRED PowerShell syntax:**
```powershell
# Directory operations
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path "folder"
Get-ChildItem -Recurse
Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "folder"

# Command separation (one per line)
command1
if ($?) { command2 }

# Virtual environment
build_venv\Scripts\activate
```

**Rule enforcement:** Any output with Linux syntax or Unicode emojis will be rejected.

## 🪟 CRITICAL: Windows-Only Repository Rules

**🚫 ABSOLUTE BAN on Unix/Linux assumptions:**
- This is a **Windows-only MCP server** - no Linux support
- **.exe files are Windows executables** - they don't run on Linux
- **No Unix shell scripts (.sh)** - pointless and confusing for Windows-only project
- **No cross-platform wrappers** - repository integrates with Windows hardware only

**✅ REQUIRED Windows-only patterns:**
- Use Windows .exe files from `integrations/` folder
- Use Windows batch files (.bat) and PowerShell scripts (.ps1)
- Repository structure assumes Windows environment
- Hardware integrations are Windows-specific (USB webcams, Windows APIs)

**🚫 NEVER create:**
- Unix shell scripts (.sh files)
- Linux command syntax in scripts
- Cross-platform compatibility layers
- Unix-style wrappers for Windows .exe files

**Repository is Windows-only MCP server with Windows hardware integration. No Unix/Linux support.**
